---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
---
<Layout title="A little clarity about privacy"><section class="shell py-14"><article class="max-w-2xl"><span class="eyebrow">Your support, your choice</span><h1 class="serif text-5xl mt-4 mb-8">Choose how you show up.</h1><div class="space-y-6 text-sm muted"><p><strong class="text-ink">Anonymous:</strong> Feedme does not attach an AT Protocol identity to your tip. Payment providers and the recipient may still see the billing information needed to process it.</p><p><strong class="text-ink">Private:</strong> Your verified DID, amount, and note are available to the creator through private storage. They are not published as a public acknowledgment.</p><p><strong class="text-ink">Public:</strong> You explicitly publish your DID, the project, amount, and timestamp on the open network. Public records can be indexed and copied. Removing a record later cannot remove every copy.</p><p>Your note is always private. Public totals include only public tips. Private and anonymous tips do not contribute to public counters.</p><p>Habitat spaces restrict access; they are not end-to-end encrypted. This server keeps an operational copy of the records. The instance operator controls that server. Live mode encrypts the local stored values with an operator-provided key.</p><p>Stripe hosts checkout and stores billing details. Feedme stores payment references and status, never your full card number. Necessary cookies keep you signed in and bind forms to your browser. There are no analytics or advertising cookies in this application.</p><p>Project images from external URLs and the Bluesky links you follow may contact other servers. Operators should publish their own contact details, retention schedule, and payment terms before accepting real support.</p></div></article></section></Layout>
